{:edb/db-before-t 2659 :edb/db-after-t 2660 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535972 50 #inst "2026-10-09T11:57:24.211Z" 13194139535972 true] [17592186198313 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377396 13194139535972 true] [17592186198322 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377403 13194139535972 true] [17592186198322 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377410 13194139535972 true] [17592186198879 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535972 true] [17592186198879 1100 "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x+y}4z\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le x}.\n$$" 13194139535972 true] [17592186198879 1100 "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$∬_(D)[∫_{0}^{x + y}4zdz]dA$\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n$D = {(x, y): 0 \\le x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le x}$." 13194139535972 false] [17592186198879 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x+y}4z\\,dz]dA & ={∬}_{D}[2{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=x+y}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2((x+y)^{2}-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{x}^{2}y+2x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}(x-0)+2x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{2}{3}({x}^{3}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{14}{3}{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{7}{6}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}({1}^{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535972 true] [17592186198882 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535972 true] [17592186198882 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$∭_(R)30xdV$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type I region given by\n$R = {(x, y, z): 0 \\le x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le 1 - x, 0 \\le z \\le 1 - x - y}$." 13194139535972 false] [17592186198882 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}30x\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type I region given by \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-x-y}.\n$$" 13194139535972 true] [17592186198882 1145 "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}30x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x-y}30x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x-y}30x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x-y}30x\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}[30xz]_{z=0}^{z=1-x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x(1-x-y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x-30{x}^{2}-30xy\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x-30{x}^{2}-30xy\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x-30{x}^{2}-30xy\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[30xy-30{x}^{2}y-15x{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1-x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}30x(1-x)-30{x}^{2}(1-x)-15x(1-x)^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+15x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+15x\\,dx & ={[\\frac{15}{4}{x}^{4}-10{x}^{3}+\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{15}{4}-10+\\frac{15}{2})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377396 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377397 13194139535972 true] [17592186377396 1089 "q-161488" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377396 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535972 true] [17592186377396 1100 "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+y}}2z\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}.\n$$" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377396 1113 #uuid "0009bcce-6e01-5a84-a1f7-a258d2553d7c" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377396 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+y}}2z\\,dz]dA & ={∬}_{D}[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{x+y}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x+y\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x+y\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}x+y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}x+y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[xy+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y={x}^{2}}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{4}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{10}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377397 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377398 13194139535972 true] [17592186377397 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377399 13194139535972 true] [17592186377397 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377400 13194139535972 true] [17592186377397 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377401 13194139535972 true] [17592186377397 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377402 13194139535972 true] [17592186377397 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535972 true] [17592186377397 1041 "selection" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377397 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377399 13194139535972 true] [17592186377397 1110 #uuid "b1b408c9-e40b-5275-834e-9e3147937942" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377398 1034 "\\frac{9}{10}" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377398 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535972 true] [17592186377398 1111 #uuid "d93faf01-991d-51e3-8236-844afb9915c7" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377399 1034 "\\frac{7}{20}" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377399 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535972 true] [17592186377399 1111 #uuid "31cebca5-0c8e-5cea-924a-e88cdac49051" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377400 1034 "\\frac{3}{5}" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535972 true] [17592186377400 1111 #uuid "5abb14df-61c6-5287-9d4d-4c5c8ffda741" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377401 1034 "2" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377401 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535972 true] [17592186377401 1111 #uuid "4e460218-3cc5-5f89-acfd-95fb5dae3c56" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377402 1034 "1" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377402 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535972 true] [17592186377402 1111 #uuid "83fe33a9-cdcf-508a-b12c-851fd20be89f" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377403 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377404 13194139535972 true] [17592186377403 1089 "q-161514" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377403 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535972 true] [17592186377403 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/330b550b31987e29aceb4b2a253e26ebec470692a6a0144f64725801f2df2b7d.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}x\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above. \n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377403 1113 #uuid "6452405b-e1dd-5ae2-81b6-5cbbf8a1c501" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377403 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/03a91dfd9f6a69455157c47162b11cd69cb3b03cfabea2770b94f7322015b0e2.png)\n\n \nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+2y},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/ac3eafe926b84588703bb8a56a1529ebe1352d25764a523b97c684a4f4e95201.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+2y}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+2y}x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+2y}x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+2y}x\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[xz]_{z=0}^{z=1+2y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(1+2y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(1+2y)\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(1+2y)\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x[y+{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}6x\\,dx & =[3{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377404 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377405 13194139535972 true] [17592186377404 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377406 13194139535972 true] [17592186377404 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377407 13194139535972 true] [17592186377404 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377408 13194139535972 true] [17592186377404 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377409 13194139535972 true] [17592186377404 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535972 true] [17592186377404 1041 "selection" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377404 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377405 13194139535972 true] [17592186377404 1110 #uuid "d22d7a49-a0a3-5e36-87ee-64c4d247f33e" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377405 1034 "12" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377405 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535972 true] [17592186377405 1111 #uuid "81e56d5d-939a-5351-8fe4-a2542fae9dfd" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377406 1034 "20" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377406 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535972 true] [17592186377406 1111 #uuid "e29e605b-eb4b-57fe-949a-99a838e72058" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377407 1034 "10" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377407 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535972 true] [17592186377407 1111 #uuid "b86f6365-6af8-5fe9-ba9d-b0fe18ca9237" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377408 1034 "6" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377408 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535972 true] [17592186377408 1111 #uuid "7b7c6f93-c9d5-5eeb-8a20-f7643e28c8c7" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377409 1034 "24" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377409 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535972 true] [17592186377409 1111 #uuid "e0abc0ea-15ae-5030-8512-fad06da9d2ab" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377410 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377411 13194139535972 true] [17592186377410 1089 "q-161517" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377410 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535972 true] [17592186377410 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/89fba52c9a48d4f8f2ddac0b060c3ffab7e3ba4f6652124f4a9ac6ba39a579e5.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}(3x-1)\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377410 1113 #uuid "4d3d9e94-e68a-5c9a-8df0-3e8abb69376b" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377410 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/86c1bef04ebf536b10f3f7d61eafcff909bd439b7641cbfc31cecd05cca23c18.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-x+y},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/dfa0a80bc323401f050d1302dc42c92558d8b566d9b0f985e955d34eb5cc15bd.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-x+y}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(3x-1)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x+y}(3x-1)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x+y}(3x-1)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x+y}(3x-1)\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-1)[z]_{z=0}^{z=2-x+y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-1)(2-x+y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3xy-y-3{x}^{2}+7x-2\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3xy-y-3{x}^{2}+7x-2\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-1)y+(-3{x}^{2}+7x-2)\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{3x-1}{2}\\,{y}^{2}+(-3{x}^{2}+7x-2)y]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2(3x-1)+2(-3{x}^{2}+7x-2)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-6{x}^{2}+20x-6\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}-6{x}^{2}+20x-6\\,dx & =[-2{x}^{3}+10x-6x]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(-2+10-6)-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535972 true] [17592186377411 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377412 13194139535972 true] [17592186377411 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377413 13194139535972 true] [17592186377411 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377414 13194139535972 true] [17592186377411 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377